{"slug":"juiced-2-ps2","title":"Juiced 2 (PS2)","desc":"PS2, THQ 2007 (Hot Import Nights)","notes":["Juiced 2: Hot Import Nights for PS2 (SLUS_215.93), read from CARS.JFS / CARS.JFH with juiced2_ps2.py: archives inside the archive (<car>.jfh + <car>.jfs per car), the PC model trees (.boh) and materials (.pmd), PS2 meshes (.p2m: VIF packets, one triangle strip per batch, the restart flag in w) and 4 bit palette pictures in the GS swizzle (uploaded as 32 bit, read as PSMT4).  78 cars, folder names = the PC archive names.","A car: chassis, the stock bonnet, bumpers, spoiler and side skirts (<CAR>_<PART>_L0) and the wheel WHEEL_<CAR>_L0 on the 4 wheel nodes.","KITS: the kit parts of the PS2 archives (bonnets, front / rear bumpers, side skirts, spoilers, one boot lid of the audi_tt: <CAR>_<PART>_VS<n>_L0 / _WIDE<n>_L0; the PS2 has no kit mirrors, roofs or exhausts) are in the hidden 'Variants' folder of <car>.fbx (a subfolder per part) and, to be seen, in <car>_kits.fbx: the stock car and one complete car per kit number (kit_vs<n> / kit_wide<n>), all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.","RIMS: _Rims holds the rims of the shop (the shared archive: rim, inner tyre with the brake disc and the tyre, the best of their detail levels) and the stock wheel of every car (stock_<car>), one per folder, unscaled, standing on the ground, outer face towards +X.","Paint: the PS2 body pictures are grey maps multiplied with the paint colour: one red here.  Lamp glows left out.  The PS2 models are simpler than the PC ones (see ../Juiced 2).  CARS.JFS also holds second / third copies of some cars (rival versions) and <car>_ui menu copies: not used."],"tags":["juiced-2-ps2"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["200sx","",1984434,"juiced-2-ps2","car-200sx.zip","thumbs/juiced-2-ps2/cars/car-200sx.webp"],["206","",2515711,"juiced-2-ps2","car-206.zip","thumbs/juiced-2-ps2/cars/car-206.webp"],["3000gt","",1747356,"juiced-2-ps2","car-3000gt.zip","thumbs/juiced-2-ps2/cars/car-3000gt.webp"],["300z